<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices firm on poor arrivals.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices firm on poor arrivals.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices firmed in central Indian markets on Wednesday against poor arrivals despite it being the peak season, dealers said.</p>
<p>Arrivals were around 1,000 tonnes on Wednesday against 20,000 tonnes per day at the same time last year, with farmers holding back stocks to get better prices.</p>
<p>Dealers said soybean prices rose by 50 rupees per tonne on firm undertone. Soyoil prices remained firm on very tight supply from plants and refineries with prices rising by 300 rupees per tonne. Business volumes were limited and undertone strong.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices gained by 50 rupees per tonne in local markets. Prices were steady in export.</p>
<p>Soymeal yellow was $278 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was $127-128 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,350 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,300-4,325 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
